{
  "dom_id": "step-q76841",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "If $m∠A=(3x+1)^{∘}$ and $m∠B=(4x-9)^{∘},$ find a value of $x$ that satisfies $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B.$  Suppose that both $∠A$ and $∠B$ are acute.",
  "worked_solution": "If both angles are acute and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B,$ then the angles $∠A$ and $∠B$ must be complementary, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+1)^{∘}+(4x-9)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ (7x-8)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 7x-8 & =90 \\\\ 7x & =98 \\\\ x & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
